                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 64,
                            "last_played": 1781436044
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "WOW! Super addictive multiplayer game! PERFECT FOR PARTIES!\n\nPROS\n- Soundtrack is fantastic and fits the nature of the game perfectly\n- Concept is ultra-simple - an old woman who's never played a game before could understand it\n- Highly addictive - I just meant to try it out but played vs CPU for a full hour. \n- Self-balancing - the more powerful our character gets, the larger you, making you an increasingly easy target\n- Super polished experience overall, lots of options to toggle and game modes to try\n\nCONS\n- Lacks descriptions of the game modes\n- Took me a while to realize which button toggled the charge mechanic\n- Maybe it's just me, but I actually played better when ignoring the charge mechanic for the most part. Might be for advanced players only.\n- Wish it had some kind of single player campaign! \n\nOVERALL: 4.5 out of 5.0. This is PERFECT for parties. Doesn't require too much thought or commitment, but shockingly addictive in its simplicity.",
